the overwhelming part of
the costs that you're

00:39:38.901 --> 00:39:41.330
facing is the storage costs
which can be enormous.

00:39:41.331 --> 00:39:42.950
So, you want to drive
that storage costs

00:39:42.951 --> 00:39:45.600
down appropriate with the level

00:39:45.601 --> 00:39:48.160
of heat that you
find in your data.

00:39:49.050 --> 00:39:53.080
So, that's how you make
a good cost performance.

00:39:53.081 --> 00:39:55.960
So, couple of caveats.

00:39:55.961 --> 00:39:58.605
Our numbers are
approximate, right?

00:39:58.606 --> 00:40:00.815
So, all of this

00:40:00.816 --> 00:40:02.530
and I'll show you how
