00:53:21.861 --> 00:53:23.420
get to the data cashing

00:53:23.421 --> 00:53:26.775
store one form or another
and it has this long path,

00:53:26.776 --> 00:53:28.660
then most of the cost is going

00:53:28.661 --> 00:53:30.110
to be consumed in
the application,

00:53:30.111 --> 00:53:32.510
and so maybe the
data management cost

00:53:32.511 --> 00:53:34.190
don't matter all
that much anyway.

00:53:34.191 --> 00:53:36.180
But I don't think
you can think that.

00:53:36.181 --> 00:53:37.210
I don't- I think that's

00:53:37.211 --> 00:53:39.940
a- if you go down
that path too far,

00:53:39.941 --> 00:53:43.095
we end up saying cost
doesn't matter any place.

00:53:43.096 --> 00:53:45.765
So, you need to start taking

00:53:45.766 --> 00:53:49.430
costs seriously
everywhere, right?

00:53:49.431 --> 00:53:52.340
One of the things
the hackathon people found,

00:53:52.341 --> 00:53:55.730
was they did this storage engine

00:53:55.731 --> 00:53:56.780
which was an enormously

00:53:56.781 --> 00:53:59.085
faster than anything
that they had before.

00:53:59.086 --> 00:54:00.860
Then they found, well,you know we

00:54:00.861 --> 00:54:03.770
have the performance
impact of that on

00:54:03.771 --> 00:54:08.550
the whole database engine
is 15 percent, right?

00:54:08.551 --> 00:54:09.835
Or 20 percent, right?

00:54:09.836 --> 00:54:13.795
You need to be able to
attack the entire path

00:54:13.796 --> 00:54:16.040
in order to be able to
have a significant impact

00:54:16.041 --> 00:54:17.810
on overall performance,

00:54:17.811 --> 00:54:19.160
and that's true costs as well.

00:54:19.161 --> 00:54:23.425
So, but I don't do
the rest of the stack so

00:54:23.426 --> 00:54:25.920
like we're only talking
about data management.

00:54:25.921 --> 00:54:28.780
So, thank you all for listening.

